Better Changes adapts behavior and code from Herdr Desktop's shipped Changes mod.
Better Files adapts behavior and code from Herdr Desktop's shipped Files mod.
Herdr Desktop is available at https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr-app and is
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Better Sidebar adapts code from Herdr Desktop's shipped spaces and agents mods.
Its bundled navigation and pull-request SVG icons are also adapted from
Herdr Desktop.

Better Tabs adapts Herdr Desktop's shipped tabs mod through the former Factory
Tabs clone. Its bundled close, spinner, file, changes, and window-control SVG
icons are adapted from Herdr Desktop as well. It adds configurable toolbar
actions, trusted local hooks, an opt-in shared button registry, and overflow.

Branch PR extracts the pull-request integration originally developed in
herdr-workflow by Tawsif Aqib, including its native UI, GitHub CLI Go bridge,
agent actions, and tests. Its bundled UI SVG icons are adapted from Herdr
Desktop's icon set.

Better Icons bundles icons from the Material Icon Theme for VS Code, version
5.40.0, copyright (c) 2025 Material Extensions, licensed under the MIT License
(https://github.com/material-extensions/vscode-material-icon-theme). The
licence text ships beside them as LICENSE-material-icon-theme.txt.

This distribution adds tree/flat file lists, staging controls, reusable diff
tabs, inline/split views, configurable typography, right-aligned space branches,
standalone GitHub CLI pull-request status, documentation, and tests.

My Sidebar

This mod is a modified copy of Better Sidebar 3.3.0 from
https://github.com/munza/herdr-mods (commit ffbdb6d), changed by Jay Stotz:
spaces roll up their tabs, agents and child spaces; spaces sort into named groups
with pinned spaces; spaces nest under other spaces; and the mod has its own space
and group menus. Modified files are views/spaces.js, views/lists.js, views/ui.js,
views/agents.js, main.js and mod.json; added files are git/groups.js, views/space-menu.js, views/group-prompt.js,
views/space-picker.js and three icons.
